{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03449",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.74,
      "end_seconds": 7.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.03,
      "end_seconds": 14.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "yes, come in and sit down what brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.9,
      "end_seconds": 22.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "I wanted to get a sudden severe tummy pain looked at"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.14,
      "end_seconds": 26.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.02,
      "end_seconds": 34.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "I'd say six months. Actually, no, closer to to about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.0,
      "end_seconds": 47.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.31,
      "end_seconds": 62.03,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "I notice it more with movement. Only lying still, and it's not much. There's vomiting as well. Oh, about vomiting, I'd call it moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.1,
      "end_seconds": 73.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.09,
      "end_seconds": 80.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "I've had gout for two years now. Yes, an irregular heartbeat"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.82,
      "end_seconds": 86.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "okay, I can see gout in your file as well. And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.79,
      "end_seconds": 90.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.12,
      "end_seconds": 94.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.95,
      "end_seconds": 99.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.37,
      "end_seconds": 119.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "what do you take on a a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.03,
      "end_seconds": 123.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Apixaban, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.67,
      "end_seconds": 126.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Okay, do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.72,
      "end_seconds": 132.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "5 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.04,
      "end_seconds": 136.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.19,
      "end_seconds": 143.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "yeah, you know, my aunt has rheumatoid arthritis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.06,
      "end_seconds": 148.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Any fever, blood in the vomit or diarrhoea at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.39,
      "end_seconds": 154.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "I haven't had fever, blood in the vomit or diarrhoea, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.67,
      "end_seconds": 160.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.08,
      "end_seconds": 163.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "no, uh, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.92,
      "end_seconds": 169.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.96,
      "end_seconds": 171.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "skin's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.68,
      "end_seconds": 176.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.77,
      "end_seconds": 186.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "okay, this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.93,
      "end_seconds": 218.62,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "okay: oxygen saturation is 96 percent, weight 61 kilos, temp 36.9 degrees, height 168 centimetres, BP is 125 over 78, BMI works out to 21.6, pulse is 120 beats a minute"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.39,
      "end_seconds": 221.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.41,
      "end_seconds": 225.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Okay, we'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.85,
      "end_seconds": 230.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.82,
      "end_seconds": 233.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.94,
      "end_seconds": 260.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Your tummy is rigid like a board and very tender everywhere, and you are lying completely still."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.91,
      "end_seconds": 268.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.75,
      "end_seconds": 290.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like a perforated stomach ulcer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.16,
      "end_seconds": 294.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.08,
      "end_seconds": 324.62,
      "duration_seconds": 29.54,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a perforated stomach ulcer, but I'd like to confirm. I'm sending you for urgent blood tests because of acute abdomen. I'm sending you for an erect chest X-ray because of possible perforation. Let's get a CT scan, for possible perforation. Nothing to eat or drink, you need an operation urgently. We'll refer you to the surgical team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.89,
      "end_seconds": 331.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.99,
      "end_seconds": 335.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "that's fine by me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.87,
      "end_seconds": 339.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "I'll want another look straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.49,
      "end_seconds": 343.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.4,
      "end_seconds": 348.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.78,
      "end_seconds": 352.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}